    "text": "Explain the difference between a CPU and a GPU in three clear bullet points. - **CPU (Central Processing Unit)**: Manages all the tasks and instructions in a computer, executing one instruction at a time. It is designed for sequential processing and is not optimized for parallel tasks.\n- **GPU (Graphics Processing Unit)**: Specialized for handling parallel tasks, such as rendering graphics and processing large amounts of data simultaneously. It is designed to perform many calculations and operations in parallel, making it highly efficient for tasks that can be broken down into smaller, independent tasks. - **CPU vs GPU**: The CPU is better suited for complex, sequential tasks, while the GPU excels at performing many simple tasks in parallel,",
